  "_note": "RUN 2 of the series -- REPLICATION of the project's first experiment with the matured instrument. The DESIGN is deliberately unchanged from that run (4 dwell levels u06/u10/u14/u18 = 6/10/14/18s per mid, adv 1s, 20 windows/cell, interleaved): the point is to re-ask the original question with the fixed two-tier poller and the offline resweep, not to improve the design. The one deviation is replication count -- 24 cells/level here against the original's 30 -- traded for wall time; 480 keys/level is far more than the endpoint needs. The original reported 40.0% live vs 99.5% offline and a false 'longer dwell delivers better' trend that was queue-pressure artifact; if the instrument is sound this returns flat at ~99.5% with live and offline agreeing to within a key or two. That agreement is the run's actual deliverable. It runs second rather than first because every run's deliverability comes from the offline resweep regardless; what this validates is the interpretation of the live series and the propagation figures, both re-readable after the fact. ~6.9h transmit. NOTE dwell and broadcasts-per-key co-vary here (fixed adv) -- inherited from the original design, which is why this run replicates rather than discriminates. Ground truth: resweep.py. ANCHOR CELLS: cells named a###_ref are the series' shared reference condition (incremental, adv 1s, 8s dwell, 20 windows, +9 dBm) -- the same cell the density matrix repeats 120 times. One opens every run and one follows every few blocks, ~10% of the run. They are not part of this matrix's design; they exist so any two nights can be compared against a condition they actually share, and so a night whose ambient density was unusual announces itself instead of silently biasing the comparison. Analyse them across runs first, then read the run's own contrast. ANTENNA STATE: directional antenna FITTED -- the series BASELINE state. Runs 1, 3 and 4 all use it, so their anchor cells form one comparable chain; only the txpower_dwell_noant half departs from it. If you run this with the antenna off, its anchors do NOT compare against the rest of the series -- record it and say so.",
